# Marketing site environment.
# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same three in the
# Vercel project settings for preview and production.
#
# Without these the collector at /api/collect accepts requests and discards
# them, so the site works normally and simply records nothing. That is
# deliberate: a missing env var in a preview deploy must never show a visitor a
# failed request.

# ── Supabase: the SAME project the ERP and Dashboard use ───────────────────
# Found under Project Settings > API. The service role key bypasses RLS, so it
# is server-only and must never be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ or referenced from a
# client component.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Analytics salt ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
#
# Mixed into the daily visitor hash so that knowing someone's IP is not enough
# to reproduce their anonymous id. Rotating this value permanently breaks the
# link between past and future anonymous visitors, which is a privacy
# improvement but will double-count returning visitors on the day you do it.
ANALYTICS_SALT=
